==Evolution==
Evolves into '''True Valkyrie Cat''' at Level 10.

Evolves into '''Holy Valkyrie Cat''' at level 20 after completing [[Into the Future]] Chapter 2.

==Strategy/Usage==
Valkyrie Cat is very useful for [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 3 and the early stages of [[Stories of Legend]] and [[Into the Future]]. However, she can later be replaced by [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]]. She is one of the first ranged attackers to deal area damage, which makes her a valuable asset in attacking groups of enemies while staying relatively safe in the back. While she might not be as fast as other units, be careful when to summon her, as it can lead her right into a boss' attack. It's best to summon her before or about when the boss spawns so that she can line up with other cats.

==='''True Form'''===
Unfortunately, Valkyrie Cat's True Form doesn't improve her stats enough to be relevant again outside of 4-Crown stages, which she is outclassed by due to [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] existing, both of whom are much easier to stack and have higher range than her, not even mentioning their [[True Form]]s. More importantly she gains a chance to Freeze all Traited enemies aside Metals, which comes in handy for [[Tiny Horns (Deadly)|Tiny Horns]] and the variant stages of Crazed Cow. This can also be used to Freeze [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies, which is irreplaceable early on into the game provided you do not have [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Vendor Cat & Kitten]].

==='''Talents'''===
Valkyrie Cat's Talents finally breathe new life into her, at last letting her serve a role beyond the earliest stages of the game. Most importantly, '''Attack Buff''' and '''Defense Buff''' grant her stats worthy of a unit of her cost, boosting each by a whole 80%. '''Attack Up''' improves her attack power even further, with her surpassing 10k DPS while strengthened at Level 30. '''Cost Down''' is not as important, but certainly doesn't hurt, as it allows Valkyrie Cat to be sent out sooner. '''Freeze''' is hardly worth a full upgrade though, as it only increases her freeze by 1 second at most, which still doesn't last her entire 4.3 second attack rate. However, the first level alone accounts for nearly half of the Talent's max effect, so it can be considered a good investment at least.

==='''Orb'''===
Since Holy Valkyrie Cat is a generalist, there aren't many orbs that can help her. Attack Up only works against a specific trait. Because of this, a few Ability Orbs suit for her, Death Mini-Surge can deliver more DPS to the enemies once Valkyrie Cat dies due to her moderate health post-Talents and hypermaxed. Cash Back also works, but her cost isn't too expensive. Dodge Attack can work too, but not much. This leaves some orbs like Recharge Time Reduction and Strengthen When Defeating good choices.

